 n\nDoors at 6pm. Performances start at 6:30pm.\n\nCantor Arts Center prese
 nts Forms & Frequencies\, a Thursday night music series featuring musician
 s and sound artists from the Bay Area and beyond.\n\nJoin us on Thursday\,
  December 3 for a night of pounding electronics and unruly physicality wit
 h Xina Xurner and Tzotzona\, with live visuals by artist Christopher Richm
 ond.\n\nXina Xurner is a Los Angeles-based sadical and sexperimental music
  and performance duo with vocalist\, sculptor\, and performance artist You
 ng Joon Kwak and musician and producer Marvin Astorga. Fusing industrial n
 oise\, power electronics\, dark club-wrecking beats\, electric guitar\, an
 d extreme vocal distortion\, their body-shaking live shows unleash queer t
 rans-femme rage\, refusal\, and joy.\n\nCreating an atmosphere that feels 
 part club\, part collective exorcism\, Xina Xurner’s performance will be
  paired with live visuals by artist Christopher Richmond\, whose alien and
  terrestrial landscapes juxtapose reality and illusion\, using handmade pr
 ops\, special photography\, and varied drawing styles to present multiple 
 pictorial universes in constant kinetic interaction.\n\nTzotzona\, Astorga
 ’s solo project\, will open the evening with brown-futurist electronic m
 usic that synthesizes elements of Cumbia\, Technobanda\, house\, techno\, 
